## v2.0.1 conservative code separation (mandatory for future updates)
- Use the supplied v1.18.4 project as the baseline for this release. The first separation pass is limited to moving the existing CSS into one external stylesheet while preserving rule order and relative asset resolution. Keep the interconnected application JavaScript in its original inline script and execution order.
- Do not split JavaScript by arbitrary line ranges or merely by visual section. Before extracting a module, map its globals, initialization order, event listeners, shared state, storage/save paths, and callers. Separate only a genuinely bounded component whose behavior can be preserved and verified. Expand modularization incrementally in later releases.
- Every separation must preserve behavior and existing account/login configuration, account isolation, saved progress, Sandbox boundaries, theme/store/equipment/reward integration, and PWA behavior. Validate each extraction and report static checks separately from browser-tested behavior.

